Query:
--Description: Correct every earlier query to avoid the non-existent column `name`.
-- 1) vaccination sites (unchanged); 2) distinct county names from the site table;
-- 3) California county “identifiers” drawn from ACS (use geo_id because `name`
--    does not exist); 4) site counts by county name; 5) population by county
--    identifier; 6–9) downstream combinations now use `geo_id AS county_id`
--    instead of parsing `name`.  Each block is separated by “/* … */”.
/* 1 ─ Look at vaccination-site rows that are located in California */
SELECT facility_name,
       facility_sub_region_1,
       facility_sub_region_2
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
LIMIT 20
